<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope}>
  <.legal_page id="privacy" title="Privacy Policy">
    <section>
      <p>
        This policy explains what eventbus stores about you, why, and what you can do about it.
        eventbus is a real-time event bus: your applications publish events over HTTP and your
        clients receive them over WebSockets.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your account:</strong>
          your email address, a hash of your password (never the password itself), whether and
          when you confirmed your email, and when you accepted these policies.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What you create:</strong>
          application names and credentials (secrets are stored only as hashes), topic names,
          allowed origins, chat rooms, chat users and chat messages.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Login sessions:</strong>
          a random token per logged-in browser, so you can stay logged in and log out.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we don't store</h2>
      <p>
        Events published to topics are delivered live and are not written to the database. If
        nobody is listening when an event is published, it is gone. Chat messages are the
        exception, because chat needs history.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use one cookie: the session cookie that keeps you logged in. There are no
        advertising or analytics cookies, and no third-party trackers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        We email you only about your account: confirming your address and resetting your
        password. Those emails are sent through <a
          href="https://resend.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >Resend</a>, which receives your
        email address and the message to deliver it. We don't send marketing email.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        Nobody, apart from the email provider above and the infrastructure that hosts the
        service. We don't sell or rent your data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Your account and everything you created are kept until you delete them or ask us to
        delete your account. Deleting an application deletes its topics, origins, chat rooms
        and messages. Expired login sessions and emailed links stop working and are removed over
        time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for a copy of your data, a correction, or the deletion of your account and
        everything in it by contacting the operator of this service from the email address on
        your account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the date at the top changes too. For significant changes we'll
        email you before they take effect.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="text-sm text-base-content/50">
      See also the <.link href={~p"/terms"}>Terms of Service</.link>.
    </p>
  </.legal_page>
</Layouts.app>
